<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Haiti postpones elections indefinitely as gang violence hampers preparations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71e2ab94620de6109e093740ed19c9e5ef9ea78e8b6b01c44c7ccecac615285e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T01:06:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-haiti-postpones-elections-indefinitely-as-gang-violence-hampers-preparations" /><summary type="html">Haiti has indefinitely postponed elections scheduled for December and February, the electoral council said Tuesday, citing technical and operational requirements as gang violence continues to disrupt preparations. The delay leaves Haitians without a vote as authorities struggle to register voters and secure areas needed for the poll.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Christa Pike regains consciousness after botched Tennessee execution attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39e85be04b70d858e71a63f7db0e0d48081d69de2b3f66ddbe95567f59cbc5a4</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T23:30:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-christa-pike-regains-consciousness-after-botched-tennessee-execution-attempt" /><summary type="html">Convicted murderer Christa Pike regained consciousness and began speaking Tuesday after surviving a botched execution by lethal injection. Pike, the first woman the state of Tennessee has attempted to put to death in 200 years, remains hospitalised with severe injuries to both arms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Colossal failure: Death penalty system in America is a broken process from start to finish'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1688366480d0fa2edb2262658d658fc7e5357837e958558e445506697bb9c243</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish--4aeddd5f6ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Reed Brody, international human rights lawyer and former New York assistant attorney general. According to Brody, the botched execution of Christa Pike reflects a much larger problem: the relationship between capital punishment, institutional failure, due process, and human dignity. The technical failure of lethal injection exposes weaknesses throughout the legal architecture surrounding the death penalty, from the quality and adequacy of defense representation to the profound disparities between jurisdictions and the difficulties states face in administering executions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f2d9f2f9bff7d241c49196baca9de823ff328a817278bb7ede7bed0b3c42c00</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:05:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--0d01da482669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35e1dd5547fc0c48f07a9e74cef3f289d0c39757e0751858967c039dc9969215</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:03:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--155757afd4f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary></entry><entry><title>Paramount completes takeover of Warner Bros, creating media behemoth Skydance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5eee863fdfe8683394ff3614439aa9c905421937f2198612f1844cadfed5be26</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:23:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance--ef54048f63ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance" /><summary type="html">Paramount completed its acquisition of Warner Bros Discover on Tuesday, after a bidding war against Netflix. The deal closed following federal approval of a settlement between Paramount and 12 US states that tried to block the transaction on antitrust grounds. Opponents in the movie industry warned of job cuts, while media groups said Warner-owned CNN's independence could be compromised.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'They Stole a City' author Lauren Collins on how Wilmington coup was 'covered up'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcd3c07ffe4e6b278779d2da8eafca7080ccba2eea7bffa7eb636e2bcf30b249</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261006-they-stole-a-city-author-lauren-collins-on-how-wilmington-coup-was-covered-up--81dea464a477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261006-they-stole-a-city-author-lauren-collins-on-how-wilmington-coup-was-covered-up" /><summary type="html">The author of a new book that tells the story of a White supremacist coup in her hometown of Wilmington, North Carolina has spoken to FRANCE 24 about how those involved and the authorities covered up the event for years. The coup happened back in 1898, but was never mentioned in local schools even when she was a pupil. Lauren Collins is currently living in Paris, where she is a staff journalist for The New Yorker. She spoke to us in Perspective about her book, "They Stole a City".</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Mexico makes push for fracking despite environmental concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caf681fd9157b2d7b6f3b980f73b3faa48d4a82e87b151fdd59792881bec32a6</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:55:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261006-mexico-makes-push-for-fracking-despite-environmental-concerns--40d4a9cbfcf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261006-mexico-makes-push-for-fracking-despite-environmental-concerns" /><summary type="html">Following months of consultations with energy experts, Mexico is preparing to tap its shale oil and gas reserves using one of the world's most controversial extraction techniques: fracking. The process is already used to extract oil in the southeastern state of Veracruz, where local communities have long complained of pollution and environmental damage. But the administration of President Claudia Sheinbaum is seeking to reduce Mexico's reliance on the United States and – eventually – achieve energy self-sufficiency. FRANCE 24's Quentin Duval and Laurence Cuvillier report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Trump targets tax-free diesel as Republicans approach midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3922507d9628cbf03ac48b07fa61cd458282951738ce3795ca90263114e0d271</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T03:08:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-targets-tax-free-diesel-as-republicans-approach-midterms--32be17b93388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-targets-tax-free-diesel-as-republicans-approach-midterms" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Monday signed an executive order to ease limits on tax-free red-dyed diesel as fuel prices put pressure on Republican candidates. Trump said the move would save farmers millions of dollars and lower the cost of goods, though analysts said the change would not benefit farmers already using tax-exempt fuel.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US to execute 2009 Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan by firing squad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c853ffc697b8d024baad38fa9e63f1b2961c3ff2d4594f732854719f0d79b02</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T01:31:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-approves-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-nidal-hasan--e67cc0cf0a56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-approves-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-nidal-hasan" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump approved a firing squad execution on Monday for Nidal Hasan, the US Army psychiatrist convicted of killing 13 people at Fort Hood in 2009. Hasan's execution will be the first carried out by the US military since 1961, with the date and location yet to be set by the Army.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Quebec votes as separatist surge poses test for Canada PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2af087b95c7607268ac9954f004af9579ca3d3a2f703fc88b9a3a357f2727add</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:36:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/quebec-votes-as-separatist-surge-poses-test-for-canada-pm--438982eb3074.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/quebec-votes-as-separatist-surge-poses-test-for-canada-pm" /><summary type="html">Quebec separatists eyed a return to power in Canada's majority French-speaking province Monday in an election that could test Prime Minister Mark Carney's message of national unity to confront the United States. Carney is popular in Quebec, and the possible success of the separatist Parti Quebecois (PQ) is not seen as a repudiation of his stance toward President Donald Trump, whose trade war and annexation threats have infuriated Canadians. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>New York declares statewide disaster emergency as measles cases rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c58c32524d44bc626ac7fe471f897f1a52d567b4bfbcdbf33e2b81f875f7daaf</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-new-york-declares-statewide-disaster-emergency-as-measles-cases-rise--535ca35f113f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-new-york-declares-statewide-disaster-emergency-as-measles-cases-rise" /><summary type="html">New York Governor Kathy Hochul declared a statewide disaster emergency on Monday as a measles outbreak spreads through under-immunised rural communities, with 108 cases reported this year. The order expands who can administer MMR vaccines and comes as neighbouring Pennsylvania battles an outbreak that has killed five people.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Concerns of US interference weigh on Brazil vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a94edb46ea15ea495710736414d552a9452354c04f9f56c0175f1db988d70cfc</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:37:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/concerns-of-us-interference-weigh-on-brazil-vote--868141281be7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/concerns-of-us-interference-weigh-on-brazil-vote" /><summary type="html">Conservative Senator Flavio Bolsonaro pulled off a surprise on Sunday in the first round of Brazil’s presidential election by finishing ahead of the incumbent left-wing President Lula, whom he will face in the runoff on October 25. Suspicions of U.S. interference have been hanging over the campaign, even as Donald Trump has never hidden his closeness to the far-right former president Bolsonaro - Flavio’s father - and his animosity toward Lula da Silva. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Return of the Bolsonaros: Why the far-right surge in Brazilian elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b89217b24eb82bd01d585dcbe0ed3d81003205c459e7106d4ed9cc28f2fc71ce</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T18:44:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261005-return-of-the-bolsonaros-why-the-far-right-surge-in-brazilian-elections--907a05e0e477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261005-return-of-the-bolsonaros-why-the-far-right-surge-in-brazilian-elections" /><summary type="html">Do voters care about attempted coups? Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro is on the cusp of unseating Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in the country's October 25 presidential runoff. Bolsonaro's father was jailed over the Brazilian version of the January 6 storming of the US Capitol. Up and down the ballot, other Bolsonaros have been elected in the first round as the far right surges. Is it about incumbent fatigue? Do Brazilians subscribe to Bolsonaro's "God, Homeland, Family" mantra?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Quebec separatists vow independence vote after provincial election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca0ce5f14310bafa82129e87461ea28508461f9f06aaaf952a611a318e0e2a4d</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T16:08:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-pledge-to-vote-on-leaving-canada--1a6d962e8ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-pledge-to-vote-on-leaving-canada" /><summary type="html">The separatist Parti Québécois won provincial elections on Monday, but fell just short of enough seats to govern alone in Canada's French-speaking province, Quebec. The victory comes just two weeks ahead of a vote in Alberta, Canada's economic powerhouse, on whether it wants to begin the process of leaving the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>How Lula’s successes in Brazil may have paved the way for his presidential defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8eca66c031f5d40e7a0df3892147d1cbe9725a2f939948513f05a829277ff3</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:21:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat--860d2205f908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s veteran leftist President Luiz Inacio "Lula" da Silva trailed Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of his far-right predecessor, in the first-round presidential vote on Sunday. Some analysts suggest that the sweeping anti-poverty measures Lula put in place over two decades may have helped give rise to a growing lower-middle class drawn to the far right’s promise to get the government out of people’s lives.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Very bad result for Lula: Bolsonaro is far more effective at speaking to that growing middle class'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c4156c8f6f9c4790acbba26e5a9281423a1a3fae8fe43938b7f3f3ce6ef7cc3</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:54:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/very-bad-result-for-lula-bolsonaro-is-far-more-effective-at-speaking-to-that-growing-middle-class--d643db93c886.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/very-bad-result-for-lula-bolsonaro-is-far-more-effective-at-speaking-to-that-growing-middle-class" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Felipe Krause, the head of Oxford University's Brazilian Studies Programme. Brazil's election reflects a political landscape that has become increasingly polarized, explains Krause. And he describes the current mood as one of “tired polarization: People are just exhausted. They feel that the political class is just kind of offering more of the same". The first round reveals a significant consolidation of the Brazilian right in government. Brazil's expanding middle class is increasingly attracted to entrepreneurialism and individualism, constituencies that "Bolsonarismo" has proved particularly effective at reaching.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil presidential election: 'Bolsonaro being ahead is a surprise,' researcher says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49ce2aefc43a7cc6bc577bda5c5a79611dad7ef134ac323d160987ee978f31f8</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-bolsonaro-being-ahead-is-a-surprise-researcher-says--c5eb6a7de29c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-bolsonaro-being-ahead-is-a-surprise-researcher-says" /><summary type="html">Far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro has pulled off a surprise win in the first round of Brazil’s presidential election. He defied most polls to win with 47 percent, compared to 45 percent for leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula de Silva. We spoke to Thomas Zicman de Barros, a research fellow at CEVIPOF, the political research centre at Sciences Po University, and columnist for our sister radio station RFI. He told us that never before in Brazilian history has a candidate who was behind in the first round then succeeded in the second.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Family of jailed ex-president Bolsonaro scores big in Brazil as son heads to run-off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e09ef1e9fdb03af8eb337fa86633a0ceab99cdf9d76e743180cbb1e88285047</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T07:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-family-members-of-jailed-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-win-big-in-multiple-brazil-polls--7be57c59ddd5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-family-members-of-jailed-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-win-big-in-multiple-brazil-polls" /><summary type="html">Family members of former Brazilian president Jair Bolsonaro won big in Sunday's general election, including the right-wing lawmaker's eldest son Flavio Bolsonaro, who surpassed President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in the first-round presidential vote. During the campaign, Flavio Bolsonaro promised to secure amnesty for his jailed father.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil presidential election heads to run-off as Flavio Bolsonaro leads Lula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:775a6a65b07d11f017e96aad816f691f26dd007dd78ff6ff548e81a9506fad2f</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T00:16:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula--792d040be18d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula" /><summary type="html">Right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro pulled off a surprise first-place finish ahead of President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in Sunday's election, which heads to a run-off vote on October 25 as neither clinched a majority.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro: A profile of Brazil's potential president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8202c11e6bb05b8dccf5ae09d5c9a953a64de27b1ab37627df9ba654895c3aca</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T18:34:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261004-a-profile-of-brazil-s-potential-president--ddef5eefc576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261004-a-profile-of-brazil-s-potential-president" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee speaks to Brazil analyst Henrique Tavares Furtado about how far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro is pledging to reshape the country, and asks: who is the man behind the political persona?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil heads to the polls for high-stakes election between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c634fca50fff9787af80620399a453a01a51917362047591a12b8276a07c848e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:38:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-heads-to-the-polls-for-high-stakes-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro--00531a37ca37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-heads-to-the-polls-for-high-stakes-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Woman at centre of Cornell gang rape lawsuit targeted with threats, lawyer says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32f2d17a07e896373906adb16de88d2d02739ebf62dbbf34d260162d6f26628</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:25:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-woman-at-center-of-cornell-gang-rape-allegations-targeted-with-threats-jane-doe--374a939685ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-woman-at-center-of-cornell-gang-rape-allegations-targeted-with-threats-jane-doe" /><summary type="html">The woman who alleged that she was drugged and raped by seven male students at a Cornell University fraternity house has been the target of threats, her lawyer told CNN on Sunday. Cornell's president earlier voiced support for an external review of the Ivy League institution facing widespread outcry over its handling of the case.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Lula and Bolsonaro tied in polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94df5ec81ea117fa72a66d525ec141ffbb13baa764224fb353e845894f716b04</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:19:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls--985ac9bf96f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Mara Nogueira, Senior Lecturer in Urban Geography at Birbeck, University of London, says the tight race reflects the consolidation of two political camps, with many Brazilians voting not out of support for a candidate, but to keep the other out of power. She points to the cost of living, religion and social media echo chambers as key factors shaping the vote, alongside a major banking scandal that has so far had limited impact on Flavio Bolsonaro’s campaign.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula de Silva: 80-year-old incumbent Brazilian president seeks 4th term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:771cd56ad0744fbd75a7462699969e763bacdede99d573aaad9b78a834b581b7</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term--6f4499fd648a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France 24 correspondent Jan Onoszko tells us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro face off in Brazil presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8a642256372353e6bcb714236dc59d59693a1895d270982039eb04f70013250</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:56:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race--d6b55874ce57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the presidential race is centred on two rivals: President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator. Dr Andrea Aruska de Souza Santos, Director of King's College Brazil Institute in London, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cornell president breaks silence over alleged campus rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91c945a7371c7fb831138d0b9611d48aeb092a030cce39a93be2ac18845ec5b9</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:53:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape--cdaa86cfffd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape" /><summary type="html">Cornell University remains at the centre of controversy over an alleged gang rape at a fraternity on campus, with the university president now breaking his silence. In an eight-minute video statement released Saturday night, Michael Kotlikoff called the allegations, made by a woman known as Jane Doe, deeply disturbing and said the university must do better. Shirli Sitbon has this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Polls close in Brazil's high-stakes election pitting Lula against Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b8f9a92fabf213ec7c13408795e1ab34fac908b7e453169ba4c5d8987dc92dc</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro--de08e320fb32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians voted Sunday in a high-stakes presidential election pitting incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, following a campaign dominated by corruption scandals, economic anxiety and accusations of US meddling. The knife-edge election comes at a moment when the region is shifting to the right in line with the Trump administration.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: A portrait of Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb9949229853513a7cb93f31c7ac1b2ec760cc928f5811a212e32204638ef20b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T09:49:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-a-portrait-of-flavio-bolsonaro--a98c600b2f2f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-a-portrait-of-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians are voting for governors and lawmakers, but the biggest stakes are in the presidential race. Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the contest is seen as a toss-up between President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator.</summary></entry><entry><title>'General divide' in Brazil's elections: 'Voters not particularly enthusiastic about either of them'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a973802e499fdd865262f44eb500b9007d0f5e987b493de0ec77a0600de51d5</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:25:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-polls-open-in-a-few-hours--33059de87308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-polls-open-in-a-few-hours" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Dr Marieke Riethof, Senior Lecturer in Latin American Politics at University of Liverpool. She sees parallels with the Brazil's 2022 election even if Flávio Bolsonaro does not have the same charisma or mobilizing capacity as his father. His programme remains a hardline political agenda that focuses on security and a reduction in the role of government. Lula, by contrast, offers a more interventionist vision, particularly in areas such as education, and socioeconomic policy. It could weaken multilateralism and reshape the country’s relationships with the United States, China, the European Union and the BRICS nations.</summary></entry></feed>
